<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Oct M3 money supply grows 15.96 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African Oct M3 money supply grows 15.96 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's year-on-year broadly defined M3 money supply grew 15.96 percent in October, preliminary Reserve Bank figures show.</p>
<p>September M3 growth was revised to 14.51 percent from a preliminary 14.45 percent.</p>
<p>Annual private sector credit growth was 18.86 percent, preliminary figures showed, against a revised 18.05 percent in September.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast M3 would grow at a rate of 15.1 percent in October, while they expected private sector credit extension to come in at 18.1.  </p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over 12 months):</p>
<p>Oct 1996 preliminary M3 growth -- 15.96 percent</p>
<p>Oct 1996 preliminary private sector credit growth -- 18.86 percent</p>
<p>					   Sept '96	     Aug '96</p>
<p>M3  revised			    14.51		  15.40</p>
<p>M2    &quot;				  18.38		  19.62</p>
<p>M1    &quot;				  30.75		  31.55</p>
<p>Private sector credit growth     18.05		  17.71</p>
<p>Monetary aggregates (rand millions)</p>
<p>			    Oct '96(prel) Sept '96 (rev) Aug '96 (rev)</p>
<p>M3 unadjusted	   311.07	  308.52	   306.44</p>
<p>M3 seasonally adj.    312.69	  309.13	   308.03</p>
<p>Private sector credit 360.98	  355.70	   349.42</p>
<p>M3 annualised growth rate from base of guideline</p>
<p>			     15.81	   15.91	    17.20</p>
<p>(1996 guideline range 6-10 pct)</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
